oints. GOTA is often associated with the formation of uric acid stones, which can occur as a result of the high uric acid levels in the body. Overall, GOTA represents a clinical syndrome that significantly impacts the quality of life of those affected, manifesting through intense joint pain and inflammation.\",7\r\n8526,CARNES ROJAS,\"CARNES ROJAS, or red meats, are consumed in lesser quantities within the Mediterranean diet, which is associated with various health benefits. Dietary guidelines discuss red meat consumption, highlighting its potential link to cancer and recommending moderation based on its health impacts. Additionally, red meats are identified as a significant source of saturated fats, which can impair renal excretion of urate, leading to elevated uric acid levels. Overall, the consumption of red meats is approached with caution in dietary recommendations due to these health considerations.\",6\r\n5598,ÁCIDO ÚRICO,\"Ácido úrico is a waste product formed from the breakdown of purines, primarily produced in the liver and to a lesser extent in the small intestine. It serves as the final product of purine metabolism. While ácido úrico acts as a potent extracellular antioxidant, it can also induce oxidative stress in certain cells, which is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases. Elevated levels of ácido úrico can lead to hyperuricemia, a condition that may result in various health issues, including gout and the formation of uric acid stones in the kidneys. Therefore, maintaining balanced levels of ácido úrico is crucial for overall health.\",14\r\n11919,PURINAS,\"PURINAS are molecules that are integral components of nucleic acids and are metabolized in the body to produce uric acid. These compounds, found in various foods, can lead to increased uric acid production, which may contribute to conditions such as hyperuricemia. The metabolism of purines is significant as it can elevate uric acid levels, potentially impacting health and leading to related medical conditions.\",3\r\n14234,PHENYTOIN,Phenytoin is a medication whose metabolism can be reduced by acute alcohol consumption.,1\r\n14235,ANTIDEPRESSANTS,\"Antidepressants, particularly tricyclics, can have enhanced depressant effects on the central nervous system when combined with alcohol.\",1\r\n14236,CLORANFENICOL,Chloramphenicol is a medication that can have enhanced hepatotoxic effects when taken with alcohol.,1\r\n14237,BETA-BLOCKERS,Beta-blockers can have their hypotensive effects potentiated by alcohol consumption.,1\r\n9458,GOUT,\"Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis that is characterized by sudden and severe pain, redness, and tenderness in the joints. This condition often occurs due to hyperuricemia, which is an elevated level of uric acid in the blood, commonly associated with metabolic disorders. Gout can lead to significant discomfort and swelling, making it a painful experience for those affected.\",3\r\n12001,REFRESCOS EDULCORADOS,\"Sweetened soft drinks, including cola and other sugary beverages, are linked to increased rates of hyperuricemia due to their high fructose content.\",2\r\n11999,ALIMENTOS RICOS EN PURINAS,\"Foods high in purines include animal meats, fish, and certain vegetables, which can elevate uric acid levels and contribute to hyperuricemia.\",1\r\n11997,ASOCIACIÓN EUROPEA DE UROLOGÍA,The European Association of Urology provides guidelines for the treatment of urolithiasis and dietary recommendations for patients with hyperuricemia.,1\r\n12000,DIETA MUY BAJA EN PURINAS,\"A very low purine diet is a dietary approach aimed at reducing uric acid levels, often recommended for patients with hyperuricemia.\",1\r\n11923,XANTINA,\"Xantina is a compound that is formed during the metabolism of purines. It specifically arises from the degradation of purines, particularly through the breakdown of hypoxanthine and guanine. Ultimately, xantina is converted into uric acid, which is a key component in the purine metabolism